WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.508
- What do a 5G network in Ethiopia,

00:00:03.508 --> 00:00:06.390
a vaccine manufacturing plant in India

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.980
and a clean energy project in South Africa

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.400
have in common?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.560
They are the battlegrounds

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.000
in the US government's efforts

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.340
to counter Chinese
influence around the world.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.470
They call it Build Back Better World.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.270
- The Build Back Better World project

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:22.120
should be high quality and high standards.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.640
- This is not gonna be
easy for the US government.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.480
China has been in this
game for eight years now

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.460
and they've committed more
than $400 billion for projects.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.610
The biggest US development agency

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.970
has only $60 billion available.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.330
So they're cobbling together more money

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.270
with other countries.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.810
So these are still really early days

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.143
but this competition
is starting to heat up.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.020
To understand where this all got started,

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.700
you have to go back to Beijing in 2013.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.872
That's when the Chinese
government pitched this project

00:00:48.872 --> 00:00:51.120
to go to developing countries

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.460
and build them infrastructure.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.040
They called this effort the
Belt and Road Initiative.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.505
And the deal was this.

00:00:56.505 --> 00:00:58.500
They would go to a developing country

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.800
and offer them a loan for
an infrastructure project.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.480
And then they would send
a Chinese company there

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.690
to build the railway, port or whatever.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.370
So the Chinese government
called this a win-win deal.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.770
Countries like the US and its allies said

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.490
this wasn't a good deal.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.890
The interest rates were really high.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.240
So what happened since the
Biden administration took over

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.020
was they've developed an alternative

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.230
to the Belt and Road project.

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:20.520
They say the deals would
be much more transparent

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.790
and have better quality, better standards

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.198
and would not indebt these
developing countries.

00:01:26.198 --> 00:01:30.115
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.400
- [Stu] What the US and
its allies are trying to do

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.700
is not only challenge
Chinese influence abroad

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.790
but they're also trying to pair it

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.040
with some of their other priorities,

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.410
including climate change.

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.060
- The Build Back Better
World is gonna show

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.020
that we can grow our economies,

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.070
fight climate change

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.560
and leave a better,
cleaner, more livable planet

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.630
for all of our children.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:03.910
- [Stu] At the UN Climate
Change Conference in Glasgow,

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:06.760
the US and its allies announced
a new clean energy project

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:07.593
in South Africa.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.057
- I hope it will be a blueprint

00:02:10.057 --> 00:02:13.030
for similar partnerships
with other countries.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.090
- They also said it signaled
to the world saying hey,

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.070
China is not the only country

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.950
that will fund and build your projects.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.690
Come to the US, come to
the UK, come to France.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.940
We have these offers for you too.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:23.940
We'll give you loans

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.670
but we'll also help you find a contractor

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.110
to do these projects.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.363
We're open for business.

00:02:28.363 --> 00:02:32.280
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.790
- Now, these are really early days

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.350
and the US hasn't always followed through

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.530
on its friendliness,

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.210
even though it says it
wants to be friendly.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.550
And they're gonna have
some challenges ahead

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.500
in rebuilding relationships with countries

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.023
like France, for instance.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.540
So it remains to be seen whether
these developing countries

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.990
will actually take a serious look

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:57.823
at the American offers.

00:02:57.823 --> 00:03:00.100
But this is gonna be a really
interesting competition

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.240
between the US and its allies, and China

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.940
to see who can win more influence,

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.780
who can build more infrastructure projects

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.146
in the developing world.

00:03:07.146 --> 00:03:09.729
(lively music)

